<title>INDIA: India BHEL sees higher 97/98 investments.</title>
<headline>India BHEL sees higher 97/98 investments.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-controlled Bharat Heavy Electricals Ltd (BHEL) said on Thursday it plans to make capital investments worth 1.5 billion rupees in 1997/98 (April-March) compared with 900 million rupees in the previous year.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect to invest 1.5 billion rupees in capital in the current financial year,&quot; R.K.D. Saha, chairman and managing director of BHEL, told reporters in the Indian capital.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
